{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.QReebEigenphaseCompact","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.QReebEigenphaseCompact","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Inverse","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.QReebEigenphaseCompact.eigenphase_route_is_compact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.QReebEigenphaseCompact.eigenphase_route_is_compact","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/QReebEigenphaseCompact.lean#L121-L135","doc":"**Capstone — the q-Reeb eigenphase route is compact, hence difference-only.** Bundling the facts:\nthe sole boost block in each binding knot is the 1-dimensional trivial rep (a real scaling `q^w`,\n`trivial_char_is_scaling`), which carries no rotation angle (`no_rotation_angle_of_boost`); every\nrotation channel is compact (`deuteron/triton/helium3_boost_is_one_dim_trivial`) with a bounded\neigenphase (`compact_eigenphase_bounded`). A bounded, dimensionless angle cannot supply the absolute\nMeV scale `C_knot`; the sole unbounded channel is the trivial-rep scaling `q^w`, already a summand of\nthe master binding formula. **scope-(a)**: the eigenphase route, alone, does not close the Δ_λ\nmagnitude gate; nothing wired, no fit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.QReebEigenphaseCompact.eigenphase_bijective_on_range","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.QReebEigenphaseCompact.eigenphase_bijective_on_range","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/QReebEigenphaseCompact.lean#L113-L119","doc":"**The eigenphase inverts the character on `[0,π]`**: `arccos(cos θ) = θ` for `θ ∈ [0,π]`, the\nother half of the bijection. Together with `char_from_eigenphase` this makes `χ_λ ↦ θ_λ` a lossless\nreparametrization on the compact blocks — the angular data is information-equivalent to the character\ndata already inside `S(K)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.QReebEigenphaseCompact.char_from_eigenphase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.QReebEigenphaseCompact.char_from_eigenphase","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/QReebEigenphaseCompact.lean#L105-L111","doc":"**The character is reconstructed from its eigenphase**: `χ = d · cos θ_λ` with\n`θ_λ = arccos(χ/d)`, on any compact block (`d ≠ 0`, `|χ/d| ≤ 1`). So the eigenphase encoding of a\ncompact block is invertible — it carries the full character, no more, no less. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.QReebEigenphaseCompact.eigenphase_recovers_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.QReebEigenphaseCompact.eigenphase_recovers_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/QReebEigenphaseCompact.lean#L99-L103","doc":"**The compact eigenphase recovers the character ratio exactly** (lossless): on a block with\n`|χ/d| ≤ 1`, `cos(arccos(χ/d)) = χ/d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.QReebEigenphaseCompact.compact_eigenphase_bounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.QReebEigenphaseCompact.compact_eigenphase_bounded","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/QReebEigenphaseCompact.lean#L76-L81","doc":"**A compact eigenphase is a bounded, dimensionless invariant.** When `|χ_λ/d_λ| ≤ 1` the rotation\nangle `θ_λ = Real.arccos (χ_λ/d_λ)` lies in `[0, π]` — a bounded, scale-free quantity. (`Real.arccos`\nmaps into `[0, π]` unconditionally; the point recorded here is the *upper* bound `θ_λ ≤ π`, so any\npredictor assembled from the eigenphases is bounded and carries no absolute scale.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.QReebEigenphaseCompact.helium3_boost_is_one_dim_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.QReebEigenphaseCompact.helium3_boost_is_one_dim_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/QReebEigenphaseCompact.lean#L71-L74","doc":"**³He (H₉): sole boost = trivial `(9,)` (`2.3937 > 1`); rotation blocks compact (max `(8,1)`\n`0.8211 < 1`).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.QReebEigenphaseCompact.triton_boost_is_one_dim_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.QReebEigenphaseCompact.triton_boost_is_one_dim_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/QReebEigenphaseCompact.lean#L66-L69","doc":"**Triton (H₉): sole boost = trivial `(9,)` (`1.5769 > 1`); rotation blocks compact (max `(8,1)`\n`0.4676 < 1`).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.QReebEigenphaseCompact.deuteron_boost_is_one_dim_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.QReebEigenphaseCompact.deuteron_boost_is_one_dim_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/QReebEigenphaseCompact.lean#L60-L64","doc":"**Deuteron (H₆): the sole boost block is the 1-dimensional trivial rep.** Reported `|χ/d|` for the\ntrivial block `(6,)` (dim = 1) is `1.5599 > 1` while the largest dim-`≥2` block `(3,3)` gives\n`0.8499 < 1`. So the boost is non-rotational (1-dim) and every rotation channel is compact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.QReebEigenphaseCompact.trivial_char_is_scaling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.QReebEigenphaseCompact.trivial_char_is_scaling","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/QReebEigenphaseCompact.lean#L53-L58","doc":"**The trivial-rep character is a growing scaling, not a bounded angle.** The trivial 1-dimensional\nHecke representation sends every generator `σ_i ↦ q`, so its character on a positive-writhe braid word is\n`q^w` (`w = exponent sum`). At the substrate `q > 1` with `w > 0` this exceeds the trivial dimension\n`1 = f^{(n,)}`: the boost channel is a pure real scaling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.QReebEigenphaseCompact.no_rotation_angle_of_boost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.QReebEigenphaseCompact.no_rotation_angle_of_boost","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/QReebEigenphaseCompact.lean#L43-L51","doc":"**A boost block has no rotation angle.** If the normalized character `x = χ_λ/d_λ` exceeds 1 in\nmodulus, there is no real angle `θ` with `cos θ = x`: the eigenvalue is off the unit circle, so the\nblock is a boost (real scaling), not a rotation. Since the q-Reeb eigenphase is *defined* by\n`cos θ_λ = χ_λ/d_λ`, it does not exist on such a block. (General; from `|cos θ| ≤ 1`.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}